Joe<div>  Just taking first look. Not quite sure how to handle the googleDataTable function</div><div><br></div><div>In a simple example</div><div><div>output$line &lt;- reactive({</div><div>    </div><div>    list(</div><div>      data = googleDataTable(</div><div>        women</div><div>      )</div><div>    )</div><div>    </div><div>  })</div><div><br></div><div>where women only has 2 columns height and weight, I see that from</div><div><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">googleDataTable </span><span style="font-weight:bold;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">&lt;-</span><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre"> </span><span style="font-weight:bold;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">function</span><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">(</span><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">data</span><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">,</span><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre"> columns </span><span style="font-weight:bold;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">=</span><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre"> </span><span style="font-weight:bold;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">NULL</span><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">)</span><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre"> etc</span><br></div><div><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">the columns are inferred and the chart appears as desired.</span><br></div><div><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre"><br></span></div><div><font color="#333333" face="Consolas, Liberation Mono, Courier, monospace"><span style="font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre"> However, I have not yet succeeded in applying the columns parameter</span></font> </div><div><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">correctly if I have a third column in the original dataset. Obviously I could subset first as an alternative</span></div><div><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre"><br></span></div><div><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">I would also like to be able to replicate a more complicated example say</span></div><div><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">the googleCharts alternative to </span></div><div><span style="color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre"><br></span></div><div><font color="#333333" face="Consolas, Liberation Mono, Courier, monospace"><span style="font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">output$gvisMotion&lt;- renderGvis({
        gvisMotionChart(Fruits, idvar=&quot;Fruit&quot;, timevar=&quot;Year&quot;)
  })</span></font><br></div><div><font color="#333333" face="Consolas, Liberation Mono, Courier, monospace"><span style="font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">where specific variables have to be assigned to idvar and timevar</span></font></div><div><font color="#333333" face="Consolas, Liberation Mono, Courier, monospace"><span style="font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre">Are these intended to replace the gvis Options in time? Do they have any advantages?</span></font></div><div><font color="#333333" face="Consolas, Liberation Mono, Courier, monospace"><span style="font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre"><br></span></font></div><div>cheers</div></div>
